{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Morning, Mr Keane. Bit blowy out on the high street, isn't it?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come and sit yourself down. What's been troubling you?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Cough.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): A cough. Tell me how it's been for you.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Mornings.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has this cough been going on?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Stairs.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): The stairs, I hear you, we'll come to those. The cough itself though, how long?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Years. Every morning.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. And those stairs leave you short of breath, do they? What about walking on the flat?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Walking.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): How far can you walk before the breathlessness stops you?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Corner.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any wheeze with it, a whistling noise?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is there any phlegm coming up?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): White.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any blood in that, or any chest pain?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): You had a chest infection a few weeks back. Has that settled?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Better.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): What antibiotic did they give you for it?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Amoxicillin.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): So the amoxicillin was five hundred milligrams three times a day for five days, for that infection. Did you finish it?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Done.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Your blue inhaler is salbutamol, one hundred micrograms, two puffs when you're breathless. How often are you using it?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): When you remember, rather than every time you're puffed?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the brown one, beclometasone two hundred micrograms, two puffs twice a day. Are you taking that?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Hardly.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): When you do manage it, is it still two puffs morning and night?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): What about cigarettes? How many are you on in a day?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): About ten a day... maybe twenty.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): So maybe twenty. I won't lecture you. How many years has it been?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Forty.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Earlier you said there was no wheeze. In the mornings, with the cough, is there any whistling at all?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Mornings.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll just listen to your chest. Deep breaths. There's an expiratory wheeze on both sides, no crackles, and your ankles aren't swollen. Saturations are 95 percent on air, pulse 88, respiratory rate 18, blood pressure 142 over 86.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): The spirometry from this morning shows an FEV1 of 1.7 litres, 61 percent predicted, FVC 3.2 litres, and a ratio of 53 percent. With the long smoking and that obstructive pattern, I think this is COPD, though I'd still call that provisional.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Right.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'd like to refer you to the stop smoking service. Please use the brown inhaler properly, two puffs morning and night, and the blue one, two puffs when you're puffed. I'll see you in six weeks. And if the breathlessness gets worse or you cough up blood, come straight back."
 ],
